tests/workspace/

# v2 runtime build artifacts (packages/*)
dist/
dist-types/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.stackdump

# Guardrails dogfood output — the GENERATED layers only.
#
# Narrowed in Story 1.16 from a blanket `_agentic-guardrails/`. That blanket
# ignore made the COMMITTED layer unreachable: `history/trends.jsonl` and
# `history/dispositions.jsonl` are committed by design (they are the
# longitudinal record and DR-1's trust-metric source), and nothing under an
# ignored directory can ever be committed — so the M1 gate would have had no
# data source in the one repository that dogfoods the tool. These three
# entries are exactly the layers `guardrails init` seeds into the consuming
# repo's own `_agentic-guardrails/.gitignore` (SEEDED_IGNORE_LINES).
_agentic-guardrails/reviews/
_agentic-guardrails/.cache/
_agentic-guardrails/config.schema.json
